                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "18464725",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198042628923",
                            "num_reviews": 106,
                            "playtime_forever": 510,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 495,
                            "last_played": 1779586676
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game was frustrating at times, but ultimately a lot of fun. \n\nI would not call this a Metroidvania. There are no weapon upgrades, double jump or other upgrades. It is straight exploration, find the keys and gems type of game. There is a lot of backtracking to open doors once you find the key or symbol needed.\n\nIt is slower paced, with some action but most of the enemies don't pose much of a threat. \n\nIt saves your progress at the numerous checkpoints and every time you switch areas. There are a few sequences that could have used an extra checkpoint but overall there were enough. There are also a couple of places where you go through a long sequence of moving things around, opening doors, etc. then something pops up and kills you and you have to repeat it.\n\nThere are 3 or 4 boss fights. One of them was too random and luck-based, too easy to unavoidably get hit and quite frustrating (unless there is a trick to it I didn't notice), but the others were fine and moderately challenging.\n\nI finished in 8.3 hours. It was well worth the price, in my opinion.\n\n\n\n\n\n",
